<title>SOUTH KOREA: Two S.Korean flour firms seek 21,500T of wheat.</title>
<headline>Two S.Korean flour firms seek 21,500T of wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Dongah Flour Mills Co Ltd and Cheiljedang Corp have jointly invited tenders for a total of 21,500 tonnes of U.S. wheat by 2:00 p.m. (0500 GMT) on Thursday, traders said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>Of the total, Cheiljedang has invited tenders for 9,500 tonnes at basis over March futures on the U.S. grain futures markets including the Chicago Board of Trade, traders said.</p>
<p>Dongah Flour has invited the remaining 12,000 tonnes at flat purchase prices.</p>
<p>Shipment was set for February 20-March 20 to the south eastern port city of Pusan.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
